content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-21100; grinding noise reported at the non-drive-end bearing.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable limit is the HF-300 manufacturer's Figure 3 severity classification for velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. Provided the reported 4.2 mm/s was measured on that basis and is the highest housing reading, it falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C restricted-operation boundary and below the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary; it does not trigger the highest-severity-zone immediate-stop rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: 74 °C was reported on the housing; the manual specifies housing-surface temperature measurement. The applicable escalation limit is the manufacturer's bearing-temperature alarm limit referenced by SSP-07, but no numerical alarm limit is supplied. Therefore 74 °C cannot be classified as below or above that limit, and the mandatory priority-1 temperature trigger cannot yet be determined.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing noise: the manual has a qualitative replacement trigger independent of the unresolved temperature limit—replace both bearings as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. The reported non-drive-end grinding noise meets the noise trigger, so replacement of the bearing pair is planned even though the vibration reading is Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal: 'seal is dry' reports no visible seal leakage; it does not establish that the pump or seal has run dry. The manual's dry-running entry is a possible cause of shaft-seal leakage, which is not reported. The evidence therefore does not justify mechanical-seal replacement solely from this observation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: non-drive-end bearing wear or damage. The localized grinding noise directly supports a bearing fault, and the manual identifies bearing wear as a possible cause of vibration and elevated bearing temperature; noise alone also triggers pair replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible contributing cause: shaft misalignment. The manual lists misalignment under both high-vibration and high-bearing-temperature troubleshooting; actual alignment has not been reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible temperature-related contributor: over-greasing. This remains a hypothesis only because grease quantity is unknown and 74 °C has not been shown to exceed the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Secondary vibration-related hypotheses are impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation. The manual calls for impeller inspection and an NPSH check when troubleshooting high vibration, but no impeller damage, hydraulic symptoms or NPSH results are supplied, and the present 4.2 mm/s reading is Zone B rather than a restricted or damage zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, verify that the vibration reading is mm/s RMS on the bearing housings, measure both housings, and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Identify which housing or housings were at 74 °C and obtain the manufacturer's temperature alarm limit. If 74 °C is above that limit, escalate the work order to priority 1 within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Record as-found troubleshooting information: check grease quantity and alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller when accessible, and check NPSH for possible cavitation. Do not treat these secondary checks as reasons to defer the bearing-pair replacement already triggered by grinding noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shut down for the planned repair. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement to remove the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework. Inspect both bearing positions and replace the non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3) and drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) bearings together as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During reassembly, apply Table 5 to each fastener actually disturbed, with lightly oiled threads: M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm if removed; M16 casing bolts 210 Nm if the casing is opened; and M10 seal-gland nuts 25 Nm if the gland is disturbed. The 25 Nm value, not the service bulletin's 30 Nm value, applies to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket; the gasket must be replaced whenever the casing is opened. Do not add seal replacement merely because the seal was reported dry unless inspection or further evidence establishes a seal defect.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Achieve parallel offset tolerance 0.05 mm and angular tolerance 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After repair, repeat vibration measurements on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading. If it falls in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before another restart. Record housing-surface temperatures for comparison with the manufacturer alarm limit once obtained.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace as part of the bearing pair because the non-drive-end bearing is noisy.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing as required for pair replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Conditional casing gasket: supply one and fit it if the casing is opened. It is not automatically required merely for back pull-out removal that leaves the casing undisturbed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before lifting, confirm component weights. For any component heavier than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-111 is confirmed to be on chemically dosed service, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The supplied dosing note specifically identifies P-101 to P-106 but does not establish P-111's service.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The current conditional Zone B vibration classification does not invoke the emergency stop control. If the highest housing reading subsequently falls in Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement, pair: standard time 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours, when the motor or bearing housing is moved.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-pair replacement and alignment are both performed sequentially, the listed standard tasks total 7.5 task-hours and 13.5 technician-hours. This arithmetic covers only those two listed tasks, not additionally discovered work.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, requires cartridge seal HF3-450B and 30 Nm gland torque for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, whereas the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450 and Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts. P-111 is serial HF3-21100, below the bulletin cutoff, so the bulletin expressly directs continued use of HF3-450 and manual Table 5. For any seal work on this asset, use HF3-450 and 25 Nm on lightly oiled threads; do not apply HF3-450B or 30 Nm under this bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the manufacturer's numerical bearing-housing temperature alarm limit, and does 74 °C apply to the non-drive-end housing, drive-end housing, or both? Until this is answered, the temperature cannot be classified and P2 is provisional; if the reading is above the alarm limit, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift (C01, C15).",
    "Was the reported 4.2 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and was it the highest of the readings from both housings? These details are needed for an unconditional Figure 3 classification (C06, C07).",
    "What are the weights of the back pull-out assembly and any other components to be lifted? The evidence does not establish whether the greater-than-25 kg lifting-plan control is triggered (C15).",
    "Is P-111 connected to a chemically dosed line? The evidence identifies chemical dosing for P-101 to P-106 only, so P-111's need for chemical goggles and nitrile gloves requires confirmation (C15, C16).",
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean only that there is no visible leakage, or is there separate evidence that the pump or seal ran dry? No leakage or dry-running history is reported, so seal replacement should not be added without further findings (C09).",
    "If seal work is later added, what shaft-sleeve scoring rejection limit applies below serial HF3-22000? The manual requires inspection for scoring but gives no numerical limit; the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion is stated within instructions for pumps serial HF3-22000 and above (C10, C13).",
    "What lubricant and correct grease quantity apply to these bearings? Over-greasing is a troubleshooting hypothesis and grease quantity is to be checked, but no lubricant specification or quantity is provided (C09)."
  ]
}
